1
00:00:06,297 --> 00:00:07,424
[waves lapping]

2
00:00:07,507 --> 00:00:09,300
[seabirds calling]

3
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:13,722
[gentle music playing]

4
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:41,583
[dolphin crying]

5
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:51,342
[dolphin squealing]

6
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:01,644
Help!

7
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:03,271
Help!

8
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:05,482
A dolphin is stuck!

9
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:07,108
Help me!

10
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:09,903
Hurry!

11
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:12,363
[gentle music continues]

12
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:46,731
[dolphin clicking happily]

13
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:47,857
[chuckles]

14
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:55,031
I'm Kiara.

15
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,116
What's your name?

16
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:57,992
I'm JJ.

17
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:02,205
Catch you later.

18
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,414
Kie.

19
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:07,502
[gentle music fades]

20
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:11,339
["Half-Heart" by New Candys playing]

21
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,974
[John B] <i>Once, a long time ago,</i>

22
00:02:21,724 --> 00:02:24,310
<i>we just wanted to have a good time</i>
<i>all the time.</i>

23
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:27,313
[John B] Should I do it? Whoa!

24
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:28,481
Oh, shit.

25
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,609
[Pogues whooping]

26
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:35,113
[John B] <i>Once, Kiara just wanted to save</i>
<i>the dolphins.</i>

27
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:39,826
<i>And Pope,</i>
<i>the nicest, smartest person I knew,</i>

28
00:02:39,909 --> 00:02:41,411
<i>he just wanted to be a coroner.</i>

29
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:48,084
<i>I don't think he'd said two sentences</i>
<i>since he'd killed Lightner and JJ died.</i>

30
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:52,797
<i>♪ I don't want to lose</i>
<i>The words that you said… ♪</i>

31
00:02:57,343 --> 00:02:58,219
[John B] <i>And Sarah…</i>

32
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:01,598
-[Sarah] Hi.
-How's the little Poguelet?

33
00:03:01,681 --> 00:03:02,724
[Sarah] Mm.

34
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,185
Never better.

35
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:06,436
[John B] <i>The Kook princess,</i>

36
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:08,980
<i>who fell for the Pogue surf rat.</i>

37
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:14,485
<i>Good time all the time, right?</i>

38
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:16,821
[Rafe] All right, it's time.

39
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:18,823
We gotta go.

40
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,535
[John B] <i>We said we were out for revenge,</i>

41
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:25,205
<i>that we were gonna take back</i>
<i>what was ours.</i>

42
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:27,832
<i>But if I was honest with myself,</i>

43
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:31,211
<i>I just wanted to make it back home</i>
<i>without losing anybody else.</i>

44
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:32,712
[music fades]

45
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,424
[ambient music playing]

46
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,509
[overlapping chatter]

47
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:54,859
[hookah bubbling]

48
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:57,320
Well… [sighs]

49
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:00,657
How many?

50
00:04:01,407 --> 00:04:02,450
Six,

51
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:03,743
including me.

52
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:06,496
Six thousand.

53
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:08,081
Each.

54
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:11,584
Abdul quoted us half that.

55
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:14,045
[Zac] You're not the only one
trying to cross to Europe.

56
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:15,713
You see this place?

57
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:18,007
Supply and demand.

58
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,968
I don't set the price.

59
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:22,220
The price is the price.

60
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:24,847
Fine.

61
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,392
[money rustling]

62
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,609
[Zac] Sundown. Don't be late.

63
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:42,782
[music fades]

64
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:45,576
[overlapping chatter]

65
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:54,294
[Cleo] So, you got us
on our way to Lisbon?

66
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:55,211
Tonight.

67
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:57,672
They'll get us to Spain,
and we'll make our way from there.

68
00:04:57,755 --> 00:05:00,550
Okay. How much of my, uh,
money did you spend?

69
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:02,802
Six each.

70
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:04,721
Six each?

71
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:08,057
-It's a little steep.
-[Rafe] I remember them saying three.

72
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:11,602
That's almost all the cash, okay?
I'm trying to get my money back.

73
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:14,355
Not to waste more of it.
Do you understand that?

74
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:16,774
If this plan doesn't work,
we're stranded here now.

75
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:19,610
-Do you want the crown or not?
-Of course. What are you talking about?

76
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:22,071
Things are moving.
Groff said he already has a buyer.

77
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:23,823
We don't have time to haggle.

78
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:28,911
-Not everything's about money, Rafe.
-[splutters] Okay, maybe not to you, okay?

79
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:33,958
We find Groff and we kill him.
That's the plan.

80
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:35,752
[tense music playing]

81
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:42,008
[ambient music playing]

82
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:43,926
[in Arabic] I thought she looked familiar.

83
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:47,180
Anton Finch is looking for them.

84
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,349
I didn't see the guy.

85
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:50,933
[tense music playing]

86
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:52,435
But that's her.

87
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:55,855
A big reward if we turn her in.

88
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:58,566
Our lucky day.

89
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:03,404
[seabirds calling]

90
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:05,615
[tense music continues]

91
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:09,702
[indistinct chatter]

92
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:13,081
[John B in English]
What is this shit, Kie?

93
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:15,416
[Sarah] I guess
the cruise ship was booked.

94
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,251
[Kiara] It's the fastest way
to get across.

95
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:19,545
You sure we should do this?

96
00:06:21,422 --> 00:06:22,840
Groff's buyer's in Lisbon.

97
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,968
We don't have passports.
This is the only way.

98
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:30,264
Yeah, well, we're here already, all right.
Deal's done. It's done.

99
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:32,600
[Zac] Move. Women this way.

100
00:06:34,268 --> 00:06:35,520
[Kiara] I see the guys.

101
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:37,522
I'll talk to them.

102
00:06:39,982 --> 00:06:41,025
Yes. Hey!

103
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:43,444
[Kiara] Hey! Who are all these people?

104
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:44,445
[Zac] Driss!

105
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:46,239
What the hell is this?

106
00:06:46,322 --> 00:06:49,575
-We did not discuss this.
-The situation on the crossing's fluid.

107
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:51,744
It's supposed to be just us.

108
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:54,414
The women. Yeah. Here!
The rest, over here.

109
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:58,042
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
No, we are not splitting up, all right?

110
00:06:58,126 --> 00:06:59,836
This is not TSA, monsieur.

111
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:02,004
Sometimes the men who cross
have incentives.

112
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:03,423
See, it's better not to tempt.

113
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:04,382
[John B] No.

114
00:07:04,465 --> 00:07:05,925
We're staying together.

115
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:07,844
-John B, it's okay. Listen to me.
-Okay.

116
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:09,011
-I have the gun.
-I know.

117
00:07:09,095 --> 00:07:11,722
If anything happens, I'll handle it.

118
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:13,266
[Kiara] We just have to get across.

119
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:15,184
No. I don't like this.

120
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,019
You can be together
when we land at Getares.

121
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:19,230
-[John B] Yeah, I get it. All right?
-Safer this way.

122
00:07:19,313 --> 00:07:20,773
[tense music continues]

123
00:07:20,857 --> 00:07:21,732
[kisses]

124
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,234
[Sarah] We'll be fine. I promise.

125
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:25,445
It's okay.

126
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:26,446
Don't worry.

127
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:28,114
[kisses]

128
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:32,577
[tense music continues]

129
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:36,831
-[Rafe] Touch me again, piece of shit!
-[Pope] Hey!

130
00:07:36,914 --> 00:07:38,374
-[Rafe] See what happens.
-It's okay.

131
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:40,209
-[John B] We got him.
-[Pope] Hey!

132
00:07:41,335 --> 00:07:44,338
Stick to the plan.
Big payday coming, okay?

133
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:45,923
[ominous music playing]

134
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:49,260
[boat engine humming]

135
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:59,145
[suspenseful music playing]

136
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,337
Why is that boat going a different way?

137
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,880
-What's happening?
-I don't know.

138
00:08:25,963 --> 00:08:27,840
-[John B] Why are we separating?
-It's okay.

139
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:31,093
-We have people on that boat though.
-[John B] We need to be together.

140
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,762
-[Sarah] Where are you going?
-[Kiara] Hey!

141
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:35,097
[Pope] Can you let us know
where they're going?

142
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:36,891
-[John B] Sarah!
-[Pope] Cleo! Kie!

143
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:38,017
-Cleo!
-Sarah!

144
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,310
Get down.

145
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,020
[smuggler] Quiet!

146
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:45,441
We're… we're going
to the same place, right?

147
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:46,484
[Zac] Yes, yes.

148
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:48,277
It's okay.

149
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:51,656
We've done this many times.
Safest way is to split up.

150
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:05,628
[tense music playing]

151
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:22,311
[man snoring]

152
00:09:27,149 --> 00:09:28,317
[John B] Whoa, whoa!

153
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:32,154
[gentle music playing]

154
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:35,616
[man speaking Arabic]

155
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:44,166
[speaking Arabic]

156
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,213
[tense music continues]

157
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:02,059
Hey.

158
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:05,313
Spain.

159
00:10:13,195 --> 00:10:15,156
[Kiara clears throat] Hey.

160
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,158
Where are our friends?

161
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,243
They're right behind.

162
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:21,704
No. They're not.

163
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:24,248
Please sit. They're coming.

164
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:25,291
[boat motor accelerates]

165
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:27,835
-[Kiara gasps]
-[Zac] This is the way it's done.

166
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:29,462
[tense music continues]

167
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:46,270
[boat engine stops]

168
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:50,691
[Pope whispers] Hey.

169
00:10:51,525 --> 00:10:52,902
The boat's stopped.

170
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:59,325
[speaking Arabic]

171
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:01,952
[smuggler] Look.

172
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:03,287
[speaks Arabic]

173
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:05,581
-[Pope] What's he talking about?
-[John B] Where?

174
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,916
-[Pope yelps]
-[smuggler grunts]

175
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:07,833
[John B] Pope!

176
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:09,627
-Pope!
-[smuggler] Enough!

177
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,420
[John B struggling]

178
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:13,172
[smuggler grunting]

179
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:15,049
[suspenseful music playing]

180
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:17,802
-[John B] No, no! Get the gun!
-[smuggler] Kill him!

181
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:19,303
[smuggler speaking Arabic]

182
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:22,556
[both grunting]

183
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:26,435
[smuggler] Get it!

184
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,520
Pope!

185
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:31,482
[John B] Pope! Look out!

186
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:39,198
Pope! You good?

187
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:40,199
[Pope] Yeah.

188
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:43,577
Go get a rope! Go get a rope!

189
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:45,746
[smuggler speaking Arabic]

190
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,873
[breathily] Thank you. Thank you.

191
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:49,583
[smuggler groans]

192
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:52,503
[John B] Thank you.

193
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:54,463
[speaking Arabic]

194
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:56,090
Thank you.

195
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:58,342
-Where are the girls?
-[speaking Arabic]

196
00:11:58,426 --> 00:11:59,593
[shouting] Where are they?

197
00:12:00,594 --> 00:12:01,554
Getares.

198
00:12:01,637 --> 00:12:02,680
[tense music playing]

199
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,014
[boat engine starts]

200
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,688
[seabirds calling]

201
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,237
[indistinct chatter]

202
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:23,909
[suspenseful music playing]

203
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:26,495
[Sarah] Still no sign of the guys.
Where are they?

204
00:12:27,621 --> 00:12:28,789
[women chattering]

205
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:30,207
[Zac] Go.

206
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:31,709
[Cleo] What the hell is this?

207
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:33,210
[suspenseful music continues]

208
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:36,464
[whistles blowing]

209
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:38,466
[women clamoring]

210
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:42,219
[policeman speaking Spanish over PA]

211
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,764
-What the hell is happening?
-You don't want to go to the camps.

212
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:46,515
You want to see your friends.
Come this way.

213
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,684
-No! No!
-Come this way. Come! Come!

214
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:49,643
Come on, Sarah!

215
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:50,644
[women clamoring]

216
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:51,979
[border patrol shouting]

217
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:54,273
-Go around. Come on! Sarah, come on!
-[Zac] Go, go, go!

218
00:12:54,356 --> 00:12:57,943
-[Kiara] Come on! Come on!
-[Zac] This way. This way! Come on!

219
00:12:58,027 --> 00:12:59,361
[women screaming]

220
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:00,905
[combat music playing]

221
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:02,615
[Zac] Come on! Hurry! Hurry!

222
00:13:02,698 --> 00:13:04,492
[police sirens blaring]

223
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:05,993
Before the Guardia Civil comes.

224
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:07,828
[suspenseful music playing]

225
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:08,913
Come on! Go!

226
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:12,458
Get in! Come on, come on!
They're coming. They're coming.

227
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:13,709
Where are we going?

228
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:15,294
To find your friends. Please.

229
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:17,213
I need proof. Call them.

230
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:18,506
Driss, get them in the cars.

231
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:20,049
I'm not just getting in the car.

232
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:21,425
[Zac] Please get in the car!

233
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:23,052
Just go, quickly.

234
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:24,762
-Come.
-[Zac] Please. Please.

235
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:27,264
-[Driss] It's okay.
-[Zac] They're waiting.

236
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,558
[Kiara] We're not going anywhere with you.

237
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:31,060
[both grunting]

238
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:32,436
[Kiara struggling]

239
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,896
[Kiara groaning]

240
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:34,980
[Kiara yelps]

241
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:35,898
[Driss grunting]

242
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:38,067
-[Sarah] Cleo.
-[Cleo] Hey!

243
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:39,944
-[Cleo grunting]
-[Driss groans]

244
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:41,320
-Come on!
-[Zac] Here they come.

245
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:43,072
[Driss] Come on, get in.

246
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,950
[Zac] Driss! Driss! Come on!

247
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:47,535
[Zac speaking Arabic]

248
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:49,328
[all breathing heavily]

249
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,412
-[Zac] Go!
-[Kiara] Sarah!

250
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:51,997
Cleo, I'm here.

251
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:53,457
[seabirds calling]

252
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,836
[John B] All right.
This is it. This is Getares.

253
00:13:57,837 --> 00:13:59,129
-You guys see them?
-[Rafe] No.

254
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:01,590
Hey!

255
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:04,051
-That looks like the raft.
-[John B] Where the hell are they?

256
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:05,678
No one's here.

257
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:08,180
-[man speaking Spanish on walkie]
-Goddamn.

258
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:11,183
That's one of the guys from their boat.

259
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:14,270
[man continues speaking Spanish on walkie]

260
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:16,814
<i>Iglesia?</i>

261
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:18,399
The church?

262
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:20,609
-You sure about that?
-[John B] You think it's that one?

263
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,903
-[Pope] I don't see another.
-Looks like a big-ass church.

264
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:24,071
-[Rafe] Let's go.
-All right.

265
00:14:24,154 --> 00:14:25,364
Hey, hang on!

266
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:26,866
[suspenseful music playing]

267
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,702
-[church bell tolling]
-[Sarah] Where?

268
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:30,619
[Kiara] Up here!

269
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,162
[combat music playing]

270
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:37,877
[Kiara] Come on! In here.

271
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:40,588
-In here.
-[Cleo] Split up!

272
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:41,797
[Kiara] Go, go, go, go.

273
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,926
Sarah! You good?

274
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,219
[combat music continues]

275
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:49,138
[Sarah] Kie?

276
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:50,848
-Come on, come on, come on!
-[Sarah] Wait!

277
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:51,849
-Kie!
-[Kiara] Sarah!

278
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:52,808
Sarah!

279
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,022
[suspenseful music playing]

280
00:14:58,105 --> 00:14:59,398
[Kiara breathing heavily]

281
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:04,945
[Driss grunting]

282
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:07,281
[Sarah breathing heavily]

283
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:11,994
[suspenseful music continues]

284
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:23,130
[music fades]

285
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,886
[tense music playing]

286
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:40,773
You think I don't know you're in here?

287
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:44,568
-[shuddering] No, no, no. Please.
-[Driss] Oh, no.

288
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,654
-Come! We go.
-Please don't touch me. Please. Please.

289
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:48,364
-We go. [shushing]
-No.

290
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:50,074
[suspenseful music playing]

291
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:52,493
-[John B] I think this is it.
-[Rafe] Better be.

292
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:54,411
[suspenseful music playing]

293
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:57,039
-Pope, go that way. We'll check down here.
-[Rafe] Yeah.

294
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,041
[Pope] Cleo!

295
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:01,043
[both breathing heavily]

296
00:16:01,585 --> 00:16:03,462
-[John B] Check that one.
-[Rafe pounds on door]

297
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:05,047
-[doorknob clicking]
-[John B] Nothing?

298
00:16:05,714 --> 00:16:08,217
-[Rafe] Nothing. I'll check up here.
-[John B] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

299
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:11,387
Come on. Come on. Where are they?

300
00:16:11,887 --> 00:16:13,222
[Zac breathing heavily]

301
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:17,768
[music crescendos, stops]

302
00:16:17,851 --> 00:16:19,436
[tense music playing]

303
00:16:31,281 --> 00:16:32,783
[suspenseful music playing]

304
00:16:37,788 --> 00:16:39,164
[Sarah whimpering]

305
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:40,708
-[Driss] Walk.
-[Sarah struggling]

306
00:16:41,291 --> 00:16:42,292
Sarah.

307
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,004
[Sarah gasping]

308
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:50,801
-[Cleo grunts]
-[thuds]

309
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:54,596
A little late, desperado.

310
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,265
[both breathing heavily]

311
00:16:58,434 --> 00:16:59,810
-[John B] You okay?
-[Sarah] Mm-hmm.

312
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:01,895
[tense music playing]

313
00:17:02,771 --> 00:17:04,314
[Kiara breathing heavily]

314
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:06,108
[whispering] JJ, if you can hear me…

315
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:10,612
Help. Please.

316
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:16,076
[suspenseful music playing]

317
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:22,166
-[Kiara gasps]
-[gun clicks]

318
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:23,709
[Kiara breathing heavily]

319
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:25,502
[Rafe] Hey.

320
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:27,046
-[thuds]
-[Zac grunting]

321
00:17:27,129 --> 00:17:28,630
[glass shatters]

322
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:30,049
[Zac groans]

323
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:32,134
[breathing heavily] You okay?

324
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:33,927
Yeah.

325
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:35,429
[Zac groaning]

326
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:37,931
[Kiara] Hey.

327
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:41,018
You were looking for us. Huh?

328
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:42,269
Why?

329
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:44,730
[Zac whimpering]

330
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:45,981
[Kiara] What is that?

331
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:47,149
[curious music playing]

332
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:49,943
[Zac coughing]

333
00:17:50,027 --> 00:17:51,945
[Zac moaning]

334
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:55,199
Is this a bounty?

335
00:17:55,949 --> 00:17:57,201
Seriously?

336
00:17:57,284 --> 00:18:00,370
Hey, guys. You okay? We're all downstairs.

337
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,581
Come on. Let's get out of here.

338
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:04,666
[rock music playing]

339
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,585
[Zac crying]

340
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,046
[tires screech]

341
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:10,422
Where's Cleo?

342
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:11,757
[horn honking]

343
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,050
Come on!

344
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,677
[Sarah] You stole their Jeep?

345
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:18,180
[Cleo] Are you surprised?
That's what I do.

346
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:23,977
[rock music continues]

347
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:39,201
[rock music continues]

348
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,870
[seabirds calling]

349
00:18:56,718 --> 00:18:57,678
[music ends]

350
00:18:57,761 --> 00:18:59,763
[bell tolling]

351
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,390
[pedestrians chattering]

352
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:03,475
[tense music playing]

353
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:09,648
[Groff exhales]

354
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:16,029
My son…

355
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:20,784
He…

356
00:19:22,494 --> 00:19:23,453
He died.

357
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:28,750
It was an accident.

358
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:33,463
Terrible. [sniffling]

359
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:35,591
[Groff sighs]

360
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,012
Terrible tragedy.

361
00:19:46,643 --> 00:19:48,645
[soul music playing]

362
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,321
-[Cleo] You'll love her. She drives nice.
-[buyer] Thank you.

363
00:19:57,404 --> 00:19:58,739
[Cleo] Pleasure doing business.

364
00:19:58,822 --> 00:19:59,698
[keys jangling]

365
00:19:59,781 --> 00:20:00,949
[buyer] Gracias, very much.

366
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,912
I just don't understand the point
of the bounty.

367
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,580
We don't even have the crown.

368
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:08,498
The Corsairs don't know that though.

369
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:10,334
We did kill one of them.

370
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:12,377
They could want revenge.

371
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:15,005
-[phone buzzes]
-Bank secured.

372
00:20:15,088 --> 00:20:16,256
Thank me later.

373
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:18,383
[John B] We got some cash.

374
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:20,469
We just…
We really have to think this one out.

375
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:25,140
[Rafe] I want to let you guys know that
we have no idea where we're going now.

376
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:28,477
What is that supposed to mean?
We're in Spain.

377
00:20:28,977 --> 00:20:31,480
We're going to Lisbon. Groff said Lisbon.

378
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:33,273
Yeah, the world's biggest liar
said Lisbon.

379
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,776
What do you suggest, Kook?

380
00:20:35,859 --> 00:20:38,946
I suggest that we do something different
than what we're doing right now,

381
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:40,656
which is trusting what Groff said.

382
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:42,741
My suggestion is Shoupe.

383
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:44,159
What?

384
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:47,996
We told Shoupe we'd give him a call
if we found Groff. Right?

385
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:52,376
I mean, he's got access to whatever,
you know, cop shit, immigration intel.

386
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,336
So I gave him a call.

387
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:56,713
[Shoupe] Wait. JJ?

388
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:58,924
No, not…

389
00:21:00,092 --> 00:21:01,176
When did it happen?

390
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:04,304
Goddamn.

391
00:21:04,388 --> 00:21:06,390
[Rafe] <i>I was just doing</i>
<i>some parallel computing,</i>

392
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:09,726
<i>some redundant systems and shit,</i>
<i>and I had him look into it.</i>

393
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:15,232
Turns out they have him leaving Tangier
but not going to Lisbon.

394
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:17,401
He was headed to Dubrovnik.

395
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:18,819
Wherever the heck that is.

396
00:21:18,902 --> 00:21:20,737
And you were gonna tell us this when?

397
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:23,323
Well, right now
because he just texted me back, okay?

398
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:24,950
Um, here's the thing.

399
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:27,160
Groff was arrested once for counterfeiting

400
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:31,581
with a guy named Henrique
who owns an antique place in Dubrovnik.

401
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:32,749
[John B] Okay, you're right.

402
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:36,503
Groff says he's going to Lisbon.
That's the last place he's gonna be.

403
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:37,671
How far is Dubrovnik?

404
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:39,756
[rock music playing]

405
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:44,303
[train horn blaring]

406
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:19,171
[door opens]

407
00:22:20,088 --> 00:22:20,922
[door shuts]

408
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:22,716
[rock music continues on speakers]

409
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:23,675
Wow.

410
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,470
Chandler Groff, huh?

411
00:22:26,553 --> 00:22:28,096
Henrique.

412
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:30,974
Been a long time, old friend.

413
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,810
[Henrique] You must want
something from me.

414
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:36,521
I want to make you a rich man.

415
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:37,606
[Henrique chuckles]

416
00:22:37,689 --> 00:22:40,067
-What did you steal this time, huh?
-[chuckling]

417
00:22:40,150 --> 00:22:41,943
Is it some Etruscan jewelry?

418
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:44,780
Is it a chalice from the Crusades, huh?
Tell me.

419
00:22:45,405 --> 00:22:46,573
The Blue Crown.

420
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:48,116
[tense music playing]

421
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:51,787
You're insane.

422
00:22:51,870 --> 00:22:54,039
Yeah. Am I?

423
00:22:54,122 --> 00:22:56,666
What, you fabricated a crown
based on some old drawings.

424
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:58,710
Now you're trying
to sell it through me to do what?

425
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:00,587
-To ruin my reputation? What?
-[chuckles] Oh.

426
00:23:00,670 --> 00:23:02,881
Ricky, your reputation ain't that solid.

427
00:23:02,964 --> 00:23:04,049
[Henrique speaks Croatian]

428
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:06,426
But that could change.

429
00:23:10,013 --> 00:23:11,390
[tense music continues]

430
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:16,061
[Groff chuckles]

431
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,188
[Groff] Mm-hmm.

432
00:23:18,271 --> 00:23:20,107
Impressive, right?

433
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:23,485
You're a forger, Chandler.
You just… forged something.

434
00:23:23,568 --> 00:23:24,611
[Groff chuckles]

435
00:23:29,866 --> 00:23:30,909
But I must admit,

436
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:34,621
it doesn't immediately look fabricated.

437
00:23:36,039 --> 00:23:37,582
What do you want from me?

438
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:38,875
Introduction.

439
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:42,087
To a specialist
who will authenticate the piece

440
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:43,422
and help me find a buyer.

441
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:44,548
You mean Medici?

442
00:23:45,382 --> 00:23:48,885
She's a world authority,
and for some reason she likes you.

443
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,598
Set up the meeting
and in return I'll give you 5%

444
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:56,935
of the hundreds of millions
that that is worth.

445
00:23:57,436 --> 00:23:58,895
[tense music continues]

446
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:02,566
It's real, Ricky.

447
00:24:04,734 --> 00:24:06,027
Just set up the meeting.

448
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:09,281
Be happy.

449
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:13,702
Your ship's come in.

450
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,418
[door opens]

451
00:24:21,501 --> 00:24:23,170
[indistinct chatter]

452
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:24,212
[door shuts]

453
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,672
[tense music continues]

454
00:24:25,755 --> 00:24:27,132
[Groff exhales]

455
00:24:29,509 --> 00:24:32,179
[John B] Yeah, I'll go ahead
and just, uh… just suss it out.

456
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:35,140
-[Kiara] What?
-No, just, I'll go.

457
00:24:35,223 --> 00:24:36,183
John B, no.

458
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:37,934
I'm gonna go.

459
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:40,479
-What? Why?
-[Kiara] Just, please.

460
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:42,564
I need to do this.

461
00:24:42,647 --> 00:24:44,566
[church bell tolling]

462
00:24:44,649 --> 00:24:45,525
[Kiara] I got it.

463
00:24:45,609 --> 00:24:46,943
Okay. Okay.

464
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:49,905
Let me know if you see anything.

465
00:24:52,866 --> 00:24:54,159
[Rafe huffing]

466
00:24:55,702 --> 00:24:56,620
Tuck in.

467
00:25:00,373 --> 00:25:01,333
[door bells jingle]

468
00:25:01,416 --> 00:25:02,792
[door creaks]

469
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:04,711
[ambient music playing on speakers]

470
00:25:06,838 --> 00:25:09,925
[Henrique] Yeah, I know it's, uh…
I know it's short notice but, um…

471
00:25:10,467 --> 00:25:12,344
Look, I wouldn't be calling you if I…

472
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,430
I'm telling you, I was just stumped.

473
00:25:18,266 --> 00:25:20,644
Yeah, tomorrow.
Tomorrow would be great, yeah.

474
00:25:24,147 --> 00:25:24,981
Ah, that's okay.

475
00:25:25,065 --> 00:25:26,107
Okay, so…

476
00:25:26,816 --> 00:25:28,902
I understand. Tomorrow, 15 minutes.

477
00:25:29,402 --> 00:25:30,237
Yeah.

478
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:32,364
We'll bring the artifact.

479
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:34,157
She can judge for herself.

480
00:25:34,741 --> 00:25:35,742
Thank you.

481
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:43,875
[phone locks]

482
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,710
Can I help you with something?

483
00:25:47,921 --> 00:25:49,256
Uh, that depends.

484
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:52,133
Well, are you just browsing,

485
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:54,010
or are you looking
for something in particular?

486
00:25:54,553 --> 00:25:57,013
Uh, right now
I'm actually looking for, um…

487
00:25:57,639 --> 00:25:58,473
[plucks strings]

488
00:25:59,224 --> 00:26:00,308
This is fun.

489
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:02,686
I'm looking for a person, actually.

490
00:26:03,186 --> 00:26:04,604
A friend's dad.

491
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:07,399
I think he's a friend of yours.

492
00:26:08,149 --> 00:26:10,068
Assuming you're Henrique.

493
00:26:12,779 --> 00:26:14,197
And what's your name?

494
00:26:15,574 --> 00:26:16,533
Larissa.

495
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:17,993
Larissa.

496
00:26:19,995 --> 00:26:22,289
-Pleasure to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

497
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,042
So what's your friend's name, Larissa?

498
00:26:26,126 --> 00:26:27,544
Oh.

499
00:26:27,627 --> 00:26:28,878
Um, his name's Chandler.

500
00:26:29,963 --> 00:26:30,880
Groff.

501
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:34,968
Chandler Groff.

502
00:26:36,469 --> 00:26:39,556
Yeah, I… I knew a Chandler Groff once,
but it's been ages.

503
00:26:39,639 --> 00:26:41,474
I haven't seen him in forever.

504
00:26:42,601 --> 00:26:44,227
I was supposed to meet him here.

505
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:46,229
Like,

506
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:48,857
now-ish.

507
00:26:49,566 --> 00:26:51,151
We were supposed to get dinner.

508
00:26:51,234 --> 00:26:53,486
He said he was gonna catch up
with you first.

509
00:26:54,779 --> 00:26:55,947
No idea.

510
00:26:57,657 --> 00:26:58,658
Okay.

511
00:26:59,993 --> 00:27:02,162
Well, I guess
I have no plans now. [chuckles]

512
00:27:02,245 --> 00:27:03,204
[Henrique chuckles]

513
00:27:05,582 --> 00:27:07,334
Maybe I could give you my number.

514
00:27:08,043 --> 00:27:09,919
Then if you see him, you can call me.

515
00:27:11,421 --> 00:27:14,507
[chuckles] Do you…
Yeah, do you just want to put it in?

516
00:27:14,591 --> 00:27:15,467
[Kiara] Yeah.

517
00:27:16,217 --> 00:27:17,302
[Henrique] Um…

518
00:27:18,762 --> 00:27:20,305
-[dialing keypad]
-[Kiara clears throat]

519
00:27:20,388 --> 00:27:21,514
[Henrique] Yeah.

520
00:27:24,684 --> 00:27:25,852
[dialing keypad]

521
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:27,145
[Henrique chuckles]

522
00:27:28,563 --> 00:27:29,814
Thank you.

523
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:35,195
And, yeah, if you… see him, call me. Yes?

524
00:27:35,278 --> 00:27:36,112
Yeah.

525
00:27:36,738 --> 00:27:38,406
Or just call.

526
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:41,159
[Henrique chuckles] Okay.

527
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:43,620
Thank you, Henrique.

528
00:27:43,703 --> 00:27:45,372
[suspenseful music playing]

529
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,168
[door opens]

530
00:27:52,253 --> 00:27:53,254
[door shuts]

531
00:27:54,005 --> 00:27:54,923
[phone unlocks]

532
00:27:55,006 --> 00:27:56,007
[Kiara whispers] You guys.

533
00:27:57,634 --> 00:27:59,844
I heard him on the phone when I came in.

534
00:28:00,595 --> 00:28:01,596
Five o'clock tomorrow.

535
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:04,224
Groff's meeting somebody at the museum
with an artifact.

536
00:28:04,307 --> 00:28:06,017
-It's gotta be the crown.
-[slaps thighs]

537
00:28:06,101 --> 00:28:08,019
-Why'd I tell you that?
-Who's the bad gal now?

538
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:10,021
Looks like you're gonna get your shot.

539
00:28:10,105 --> 00:28:10,980
[tense music playing]

540
00:28:11,064 --> 00:28:13,483
-[John B] Good show, Kie.
-[Kiara] Yeah. We should keep moving.

541
00:28:13,566 --> 00:28:14,818
-Yeah. Ready?
-[Sarah] Okay.

542
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:16,319
[Kiara] Let's go. Let's go.

543
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:17,570
[rock music playing]

544
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:18,697
Five o'clock.

545
00:28:19,239 --> 00:28:21,950
<i>"Muzej… </i>Architecture. Okay.

546
00:28:22,033 --> 00:28:23,827
Go. Move.

547
00:28:25,161 --> 00:28:26,121
[Cleo] Hurry!

548
00:28:32,752 --> 00:28:36,005
[Groff] And she just happened to come
in the store right after I left?

549
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:37,882
[Henrique]<i>Yeah, she said</i>
<i>she was your friend.</i>

550
00:28:38,633 --> 00:28:39,884
[Groff scoffs] Did she?

551
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:41,803
What did she look like?

552
00:28:41,886 --> 00:28:42,887
[Henrique] <i>I don't know.</i>

553
00:28:42,971 --> 00:28:46,057
Brown eyes, brown hair, brown skin.
Gorgeous.

554
00:28:46,141 --> 00:28:49,269
<i>I… Young. I don't know.</i>
<i>She… she said her name was Larissa.</i>

555
00:28:50,019 --> 00:28:51,271
[bell tolling]

556
00:28:51,354 --> 00:28:52,188
[Groff sighs]

557
00:28:53,314 --> 00:28:54,983
What did you tell her, Ricky?

558
00:28:55,066 --> 00:28:56,568
<i>Oh, easy. I've been around the block.</i>

559
00:28:56,651 --> 00:28:58,695
<i>I'm not stupid.</i>
<i>Of course I didn't tell her anything.</i>

560
00:28:58,778 --> 00:29:00,655
<i>But she took my phone.</i>

561
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:03,783
So now we have to assume that she…
she knows about the meeting, right?

562
00:29:04,367 --> 00:29:05,452
<i>Should I cancel it?</i>

563
00:29:05,952 --> 00:29:07,370
[ominous music playing]

564
00:29:08,872 --> 00:29:09,998
No, no.

565
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:12,000
No, no, it's okay.

566
00:29:13,042 --> 00:29:14,335
It's good, actually.

567
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:18,173
Tell the great Medici

568
00:29:19,132 --> 00:29:20,884
I look forward to meeting her.

569
00:29:22,385 --> 00:29:23,219
[phone clicks]

570
00:29:23,303 --> 00:29:24,971
[Groff mutters and sighs]

571
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:31,060
[in Croatian] Hello, friend. [chuckles]

572
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:32,729
Do you speak English?

573
00:29:32,812 --> 00:29:34,647
-[server speaks Croatian]
-[chuckles]

574
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:38,067
I have a question.

575
00:29:40,403 --> 00:29:43,740
How… tall are you?

576
00:29:44,574 --> 00:29:46,367
[gentle piano music playing]

577
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:57,796
[Finch chuckles]

578
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:58,838
[in English] <i>Bravo!</i>

579
00:29:58,922 --> 00:30:00,799
[Sadie] <i>I learned it just for you, Dad.</i>

580
00:30:00,882 --> 00:30:02,383
[Finch] <i>Sounds beautiful, sweetie.</i>

581
00:30:02,467 --> 00:30:04,302
[dramatic music playing]

582
00:30:04,385 --> 00:30:05,929
[helicopter whirring]

583
00:30:09,432 --> 00:30:10,683
[Corsairs shouting]

584
00:30:15,438 --> 00:30:17,607
[Dalia] Sorry to keep
you waiting, Mr. Finch.

585
00:30:17,690 --> 00:30:18,733
[tablet locks]

586
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:20,985
The bearer of bad news returns.

587
00:30:21,486 --> 00:30:23,112
[dramatic music continues]

588
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:29,577
Who are these?

589
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:30,495
[Dalia] Nobodies.

590
00:30:30,578 --> 00:30:33,122
It's those kids from North Carolina.

591
00:30:33,206 --> 00:30:35,792
Well, they found the crown before you did.

592
00:30:36,459 --> 00:30:38,378
Maybe I should have hired them.

593
00:30:41,047 --> 00:30:43,716
What we're hearing from our sources is
Groff killed one of them

594
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:46,219
and then took the crown for himself.

595
00:30:46,719 --> 00:30:49,305
Our informant in Kildare thinks
he's headed to Dubrovnik.

596
00:30:49,389 --> 00:30:51,474
But he can't sell it without a dealer.

597
00:30:51,558 --> 00:30:54,936
When he contacts one of the big fish,
we will know.

598
00:30:57,188 --> 00:31:01,276
The smugglers, who had the girl who saw
the crown… I want to talk to them.

599
00:31:01,359 --> 00:31:02,777
Yeah, I thought you would.

600
00:31:03,486 --> 00:31:04,779
[whistles] Oi!

601
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:06,322
[Driss and Zac grunting]

602
00:31:07,490 --> 00:31:09,200
[Driss breathing heavily]

603
00:31:09,284 --> 00:31:10,785
[dramatic music continues]

604
00:31:17,208 --> 00:31:19,294
Mr. Finch. Mr. Finch, I'm sorry--

605
00:31:19,377 --> 00:31:21,212
Oh, no, no. Shut it!

606
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:24,048
[Zac] I'm… I'm sorry we lost the girl.

607
00:31:24,132 --> 00:31:25,842
At ease, friends.

608
00:31:26,801 --> 00:31:27,927
-[Zac groans]
-[thuds]

609
00:31:28,011 --> 00:31:30,471
I was a smuggler once myself.

610
00:31:31,806 --> 00:31:34,183
Dodging the police, the border guards.

611
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:36,019
Headaches.

612
00:31:36,102 --> 00:31:37,270
[both chuckle]

613
00:31:38,062 --> 00:31:39,814
We apologize, Mr. Finch.

614
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:40,982
But never women.

615
00:31:41,065 --> 00:31:42,358
[tense music playing]

616
00:31:44,277 --> 00:31:46,070
I had a daughter once.

617
00:31:50,783 --> 00:31:54,787
I want to talk to you about the… the girl,
the one that was on your boat.

618
00:31:55,496 --> 00:31:59,542
I'm told she had seen an old artifact
that I'm very interested in.

619
00:32:02,587 --> 00:32:04,172
She ever talk about a crown?

620
00:32:04,255 --> 00:32:05,924
Crown? No.

621
00:32:06,507 --> 00:32:09,218
They were looking for something.
Nothing about the crown.

622
00:32:09,719 --> 00:32:10,929
[tense music continues]

623
00:32:11,721 --> 00:32:13,056
See, that's disappointing.

624
00:32:16,517 --> 00:32:20,188
I don't like… to be disappointed.

625
00:32:21,272 --> 00:32:22,398
But I'll get over it.

626
00:32:22,482 --> 00:32:26,402
Today is your lucky day,
as I am short of recruits.

627
00:32:27,904 --> 00:32:28,780
You

628
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:32,408
can continue smuggling.

629
00:32:33,284 --> 00:32:38,373
Or you can join the Corsairs
and live a life of adventure

630
00:32:39,082 --> 00:32:40,375
and honor…

631
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:44,003
and if you zero out,

632
00:32:44,587 --> 00:32:48,091
a generous payment to your family.

633
00:32:49,676 --> 00:32:51,803
But if you prefer a coward's death…

634
00:32:51,886 --> 00:32:53,972
Yes, we'll join. Yes.

635
00:32:54,055 --> 00:32:54,973
But…

636
00:32:56,557 --> 00:32:59,143
I only have room for one of you.

637
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:02,563
[unsettling music playing]

638
00:33:13,282 --> 00:33:14,993
[both grunting]

639
00:33:18,663 --> 00:33:20,456
[both struggling]

640
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:22,000
[combat music playing]

641
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:23,751
-[Zac groaning]
-[body thuds]

642
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:26,087
[music stops]

643
00:33:27,505 --> 00:33:28,756
[gun clicks]

644
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:30,133
[suspenseful music playing]

645
00:33:30,216 --> 00:33:31,509
[Zac breathing heavily]

646
00:33:32,218 --> 00:33:33,970
No! No!

647
00:33:34,887 --> 00:33:36,139
[body thuds]

648
00:33:36,222 --> 00:33:37,557
[tense music playing]

649
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:39,434
[Zac breathing heavily]

650
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:53,698
Get him a contract.

651
00:33:55,241 --> 00:33:57,243
[Dalia] Right. Get him out of here.

652
00:33:57,326 --> 00:33:58,536
Welcome aboard.

653
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:00,705
It's an exciting life.

654
00:34:01,414 --> 00:34:02,957
[dramatic music playing]

655
00:34:10,673 --> 00:34:11,716
So?

656
00:34:12,258 --> 00:34:13,426
Dubrovnik?

657
00:34:20,933 --> 00:34:21,934
[tablet unlocks]

658
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:23,561
[soft piano playing on tablet]

659
00:34:25,271 --> 00:34:26,939
[dramatic music playing]

660
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:31,194
[Spanish music playing]

661
00:34:31,819 --> 00:34:33,154
[John B] Okay, so right there.

662
00:34:33,237 --> 00:34:36,115
That's the museum where we think
Groff is gonna be meeting at.

663
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:38,951
The only way to get to that museum
is through the gondola.

664
00:34:39,035 --> 00:34:42,121
The gondola is the only public access
up to the museum.

665
00:34:42,205 --> 00:34:43,998
All right? So I think
we need to go into town.

666
00:34:44,082 --> 00:34:46,793
We need to find some new clothes.
We need to blend in.

667
00:34:47,627 --> 00:34:50,546
We set up in three spots in the plaza
near the entrance to the gondola,

668
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:52,006
and we wait for Groff.

669
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:55,009
We go in pairs.
Everybody has everybody's back.

670
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:58,346
We good? We got it?

671
00:35:00,932 --> 00:35:02,141
Yeah, we're good.

672
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:05,770
-Let's just talk objectives, yeah?
-[John B] All right.

673
00:35:05,853 --> 00:35:08,022
We don't know what we're gonna see
when we go up there.

674
00:35:08,648 --> 00:35:11,818
It could be tons of people.
Coppers, mercenaries…

675
00:35:11,901 --> 00:35:13,277
We could be in over our heads.

676
00:35:13,361 --> 00:35:15,488
[John B] We're gonna be
as safe as possible, all right?

677
00:35:15,571 --> 00:35:17,532
But the first objective is the crown.

678
00:35:17,615 --> 00:35:20,535
Well, the crown is the only objective,
actually, okay?

679
00:35:20,618 --> 00:35:21,994
It's the only way we get paid.

680
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:24,705
[Sarah] Yeah, but if we're able to get
the crown from Groff,

681
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:26,999
can't we just leave him for the cops?

682
00:35:27,083 --> 00:35:29,210
We're not leaving Groff to the cops.

683
00:35:29,293 --> 00:35:30,503
[tense music playing]

684
00:35:31,295 --> 00:35:33,840
Okay, crown first. Death vendetta second.

685
00:35:34,841 --> 00:35:36,509
Why don't you stay out of it, Rafe?

686
00:35:36,592 --> 00:35:37,593
Guys.

687
00:35:37,677 --> 00:35:39,428
-What are you talking about?
-[Sarah] Rafe!

688
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:41,889
-Stay out of it!
-This has everything to do with me too.

689
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:45,685
-And you're going to get us killed.
-[John B] Guys, stop! Hey! We all miss JJ.

690
00:35:45,768 --> 00:35:46,853
-Relax.
-I don't miss him.

691
00:35:46,936 --> 00:35:47,895
-Rafe!
-I barely knew him.

692
00:35:47,979 --> 00:35:50,523
Really? JJ saved your sister's life.

693
00:35:50,606 --> 00:35:52,233
[dramatic music playing]

694
00:35:54,110 --> 00:35:55,695
He saved all of us.

695
00:35:58,739 --> 00:36:00,533
Why is nobody acting like it?

696
00:36:01,284 --> 00:36:03,828
[Sarah] Rafe! Please.

697
00:36:03,911 --> 00:36:05,872
Why are you…
why are you saying please to me?

698
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:08,499
[Sarah] Please, just stop talking.
Just stop talking. Please!

699
00:36:08,583 --> 00:36:10,168
-[Rafe] All right!
-[Cleo] Shut up, Rafe.

700
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:12,795
-[Sarah] I'm sorry.
-[John B] It's okay.

701
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:14,755
It's not your fault. It's your brother's.

702
00:36:16,883 --> 00:36:18,676
[dramatic music continues]

703
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:20,803
[John B] I'll go check on her.

704
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:23,306
[Kiara breathing shakily]

705
00:36:26,726 --> 00:36:27,810
[John B] Hey.

706
00:36:28,728 --> 00:36:30,229
Can I join you?

707
00:36:31,147 --> 00:36:32,940
[gentle music playing]

708
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:34,317
[Kiara sniffles]

709
00:36:35,943 --> 00:36:36,986
[Kiara sighs]

710
00:36:42,617 --> 00:36:45,244
-John B--
-I'm not here to tell you what to do, Kie.

711
00:36:46,704 --> 00:36:47,580
I'm not.

712
00:36:52,084 --> 00:36:53,044
I get it.

713
00:36:53,794 --> 00:36:57,340
I mean, I… I keep thinking,
what if I didn't go down the hill?

714
00:36:58,799 --> 00:37:00,509
What if I would've stayed,
if I'd done more?

715
00:37:00,593 --> 00:37:03,221
What if… what if
I would've just done something?

716
00:37:03,721 --> 00:37:06,849
-This isn't it your fault.
-It's not your fault either, Kie.

717
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:10,269
[voice trembling] You get that, right?

718
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:14,523
I'm just scared.

719
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:17,318
I just don't want to mess it up.

720
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:19,820
What if somebody else does it?

721
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:24,200
You know J wouldn't want you to do this.

722
00:37:26,244 --> 00:37:28,079
[crying] I don't think you understand.

723
00:37:28,162 --> 00:37:29,664
[somber music playing]

724
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:35,002
Groff killed JJ right in front of me.

725
00:37:39,882 --> 00:37:41,133
And I stood there.

726
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:43,970
And I froze.

727
00:37:45,429 --> 00:37:46,973
[voice trembling] And I failed him.

728
00:37:49,725 --> 00:37:52,353
[sniffles] And now
the only thing that I can do…

729
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:54,522
The…

730
00:37:55,022 --> 00:37:56,983
The only thing that I can do…

731
00:38:00,111 --> 00:38:01,028
is this.

732
00:38:01,737 --> 00:38:02,905
For him.

733
00:38:02,989 --> 00:38:04,323
[tense music playing]

734
00:38:05,533 --> 00:38:07,326
Whatever happens after doesn't matter.

735
00:38:07,410 --> 00:38:10,579
I just need you guys to have my back. Now.

736
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:14,417
Come here.

737
00:38:15,751 --> 00:38:17,253
I got you, okay?

738
00:38:20,464 --> 00:38:21,716
[church bell tolling]

739
00:38:21,799 --> 00:38:23,801
[intriguing music playing]

740
00:38:25,553 --> 00:38:27,096
[indistinct chatter]

741
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:35,521
[John B] Okay, just like we discussed.
Eyes peeled for Groff.

742
00:38:35,604 --> 00:38:36,439
This meeting is soon.

743
00:38:36,522 --> 00:38:38,691
He's got to go through that alley
to get to the gondola.

744
00:38:38,774 --> 00:38:40,443
-We good?
-[Rafe] Yeah, we got it.

745
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:43,487
[suspenseful music playing]

746
00:39:06,969 --> 00:39:09,221
All right, if anything happens,
just stay back, okay?

747
00:39:09,305 --> 00:39:10,389
[Sarah] I'm not useless.

748
00:39:10,473 --> 00:39:11,974
I'm… I'm not saying you're useless.

749
00:39:12,058 --> 00:39:14,393
-But you should be on a boat going home.
-What?

750
00:39:14,477 --> 00:39:16,520
Does John B give a shit
that you're having a baby?

751
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:18,939
Yes, he does.
This was my choice to be here.

752
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:21,609
Oh, good, yeah. Pogue like shit, huh?

753
00:39:21,692 --> 00:39:22,610
[Sarah] Whatever.

754
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:25,237
[Rafe] Listen.

755
00:39:26,322 --> 00:39:30,326
No matter how many dumb decisions
you make, okay, you're still family.

756
00:39:30,951 --> 00:39:32,787
That means something to me.

757
00:39:32,870 --> 00:39:33,954
I'm helping <i>you.</i>

758
00:39:35,081 --> 00:39:38,292
So don't expect me to risk my life
for anyone else. You got that?

759
00:39:39,418 --> 00:39:40,920
[tense music playing]

760
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:42,421
Noted.

761
00:39:43,130 --> 00:39:44,006
Fine.

762
00:39:44,882 --> 00:39:46,884
[suspenseful music playing]

763
00:39:51,722 --> 00:39:53,099
[Pope sighs]

764
00:39:54,558 --> 00:39:56,060
[indistinct chatter]

765
00:39:58,354 --> 00:39:59,355
[Cleo] Hungry?

766
00:40:03,192 --> 00:40:04,402
[sighs]

767
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:06,654
Can I say something?

768
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,115
Pope…

769
00:40:11,325 --> 00:40:12,243
Look.

770
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:14,412
Doing what you did…

771
00:40:15,079 --> 00:40:15,955
Taking that shot…

772
00:40:16,956 --> 00:40:18,416
You didn't have a choice.

773
00:40:19,500 --> 00:40:20,668
You know that, right?

774
00:40:22,128 --> 00:40:23,421
He's still dead.

775
00:40:25,047 --> 00:40:26,382
I still killed him.

776
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:29,301
Listen.

777
00:40:30,428 --> 00:40:32,972
We got Groff and the Corsairs out there.

778
00:40:33,556 --> 00:40:35,599
If they catch you, they're gonna gut you.

779
00:40:36,517 --> 00:40:38,227
So I need you to just be strong.

780
00:40:38,310 --> 00:40:41,605
And get your head in the game.
It's too dangerous if you don't.

781
00:40:43,524 --> 00:40:44,733
-Okay?
-[Pope] I got it.

782
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:47,903
-Pope, it's not about--
-I said I got it.

783
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:50,781
I got it. Thank you.

784
00:40:55,911 --> 00:40:57,079
See him?

785
00:40:57,163 --> 00:40:58,164
Nothing.

786
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:00,666
He should be here by now.

787
00:41:00,749 --> 00:41:02,751
[indistinct chatter]

788
00:41:03,961 --> 00:41:05,963
[traditional Croatian music playing]

789
00:41:12,136 --> 00:41:13,888
[man speaking Croatian]

790
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:20,102
[tense music playing]

791
00:41:23,314 --> 00:41:24,815
-I'll be right back.
-[Kiara] Hm?

792
00:41:24,899 --> 00:41:26,901
Stay right here. Okay?
I might've seen something.

793
00:41:26,984 --> 00:41:28,527
-What?
-Just trust me on this one, okay?

794
00:41:29,195 --> 00:41:30,905
[rock music playing]

795
00:41:56,805 --> 00:41:58,224
[Kiara] Shit, John B.

796
00:42:08,817 --> 00:42:10,444
[rock music continues]

797
00:42:30,714 --> 00:42:32,341
[group rhythmically clapping]

798
00:42:32,424 --> 00:42:33,509
[John B] Kie!

799
00:42:34,927 --> 00:42:35,928
Kie!

800
00:42:40,015 --> 00:42:41,141
[John B whistles]

801
00:42:47,856 --> 00:42:50,526
Kie went off on her own towards
the gondola. I think she saw Groff.

802
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:52,528
-[Sarah] Where were you?
-I thought I saw him too.

803
00:42:52,611 --> 00:42:55,030
-[Sarah] We gotta catch her.
-Let's go. Come on! Go!

804
00:42:57,908 --> 00:42:59,076
[music stops]

805
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:04,748
[tense music playing]

806
00:43:07,042 --> 00:43:08,669
[indistinct chatter]

807
00:43:26,645 --> 00:43:28,063
[tense music continues]

808
00:43:28,897 --> 00:43:30,274
[attendant speaking Croatian]

809
00:43:35,904 --> 00:43:37,031
[door closes]

810
00:43:39,658 --> 00:43:41,201
[gondola whirring]

811
00:43:49,126 --> 00:43:50,878
[tense music continues]

812
00:43:53,922 --> 00:43:55,007
[John B] Let's go, let's go!

813
00:43:55,090 --> 00:43:56,842
[Rafe] Did you actually see Groff?

814
00:43:56,925 --> 00:43:58,927
[John B] No, but I saw
Kie running this way.

815
00:43:59,011 --> 00:44:00,763
[Cleo] She must have gone after him.

816
00:44:00,846 --> 00:44:02,765
[Sarah] We're gonna have
to wait for the next car.

817
00:44:04,350 --> 00:44:06,143
[tense music continues]

818
00:44:08,395 --> 00:44:09,730
[indistinct chatter]

819
00:44:15,903 --> 00:44:17,029
-[Kiara] <i>No!</i>
-[JJ shouts]

820
00:44:17,112 --> 00:44:18,072
[JJ whimpering]

821
00:44:18,155 --> 00:44:19,365
[Kiara] <i>It's okay. It's okay.</i>

822
00:44:20,491 --> 00:44:21,492
[JJ yelps]

823
00:44:21,575 --> 00:44:22,951
-[JJ gasping]
-[knife swishes]

824
00:44:24,870 --> 00:44:26,246
[tense music continues]

825
00:44:37,466 --> 00:44:39,051
[child laughing]

826
00:44:40,803 --> 00:44:43,430
[passenger speaking Croatian]

827
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:50,062
[tense music continues]

828
00:45:00,823 --> 00:45:02,658
[tense music continues]

829
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:12,167
[indistinct chatter]

830
00:45:18,507 --> 00:45:20,008
[gears clicking]

831
00:45:32,646 --> 00:45:34,440
[combat music playing]

832
00:45:41,029 --> 00:45:42,823
[indistinct chatter]

833
00:45:50,122 --> 00:45:51,206
[gun clicks]

834
00:45:53,709 --> 00:45:55,544
[suspenseful music playing]

835
00:46:04,762 --> 00:46:05,804
Look at me!

836
00:46:05,888 --> 00:46:07,014
-[gun clicks]
-[server gasps]

837
00:46:07,097 --> 00:46:08,223
[server whimpering]

838
00:46:08,807 --> 00:46:10,601
[in Croatian] Don't shoot!
Please don't shoot!

839
00:46:11,185 --> 00:46:12,936
[Groff in English]
There's an American girl.

840
00:46:13,020 --> 00:46:15,981
Uh, brown hair, uh, uh, tan coat.
She's… she's got a gun.

841
00:46:16,064 --> 00:46:19,651
I don't know what she'll do.
Uh, please come as quickly as you can.

842
00:46:19,735 --> 00:46:20,569
[server] Hey!

843
00:46:20,652 --> 00:46:22,738
-[crowd murmuring]
-[server speaking Croatian]

844
00:46:22,821 --> 00:46:24,740
-[bystander] Oh my God!
-[camera shutter snaps]

845
00:46:24,823 --> 00:46:25,783
[Kiara] I'm sorry.

846
00:46:28,285 --> 00:46:29,286
Shit.

847
00:46:29,369 --> 00:46:30,287
What the hell?

848
00:46:31,830 --> 00:46:33,540
[sirens wailing]

849
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:37,503
Bye, Kiara.

850
00:46:41,799 --> 00:46:42,716
[tires screeching]

851
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:44,426
[police sirens blaring]

852
00:46:46,887 --> 00:46:48,472
[music crescendos, stops]

853
00:46:49,515 --> 00:46:51,266
[rock music playing]

854
00:50:11,299 --> 00:50:12,634
[music fades]

